# YORewards — Codebase Map

Use this to locate patterns instead of re-searching. When building a feature, **copy the canonical reference slice** below rather than inventing a new shape.

## App ownership

| App | Path | Routing dir | Features dir | Font / theme |
| --- | ---- | ----------- | ------------ | ------------ |
| Customer PWA | `apps/customer` | `app/` (route groups `(main)`, `(public)`, `(auth)`, `stamp`) | `src/features/*` | Geist · light · installable PWA |
| Merchant dashboard | `apps/merchant` | `src/app/merchant/*` | `src/features/*` + `src/widgets/*` | Plus Jakarta Sans · dark · sidebar shell |
| Super admin | `apps/admin` | `app/admin/*` | `src/features/*` | light · `AdminShell` |

Shared packages: `@repo/supabase` (data), `@repo/utils` (pure helpers, error codes, otp, email), `@repo/ui` (shadcn primitives), `@repo/tailwind-config`, `@repo/eslint-config`, `@repo/typescript-config`.

## Layering (from `root.mdc` / `fda-structure.mdc`)

```
app → widgets → features → entities → shared → (@repo/*)
```

Never import feature-to-feature. Import shared code via `@/…` aliases and `@repo/*` barrels. Pages stay thin — compose from features.

## The canonical reference slice — copy this for any vertical feature

**Disputes** is the reference end-to-end implementation. To add a new data-backed feature, mirror these files in order:

| Layer | Reference file | What to copy |
| ----- | -------------- | ------------ |
| Client-safe types + pure helpers | `packages/supabase/src/queries/stamp-disputes-shared.ts` | Types, enums, SLA math — **imports only `../types`**, no `server.ts` |
| Server-only queries | `packages/supabase/src/queries/stamp-disputes.ts` | DB reads/writes; imports `../server` / `../service-role`; add path to `package.json` `exports` |
| Server action | `apps/customer/src/features/disputes/api/disputeActions.ts` | `"use server"`, auth guard → `fail("UNAUTHORIZED")`, validation → codes, `try/catch` → `logActionFailure` + `fail(...)`, `revalidatePath` |
| TanStack keys / invalidation | `apps/customer/src/features/wallet/api/walletQueries.ts` | Query-key factory + `invalidate*` / `refresh*` helpers |
| UI | `apps/customer/src/features/disputes/components/*` | `"use client"`, `useTranslations`, `resolveActionError`, toast on success |
| Barrel | `apps/customer/src/features/disputes/index.ts` | Export only the public API |

Admin + merchant mirror the same slice under their own `features/disputes/`.

## Server actions (see `server-action-errors.mdc`)

- Return **codes only** via `fail("CODE")` from `@repo/utils/action-error`; never English strings or raw DB errors.
- Register every new code in `packages/utils/src/action-error.ts` (`ActionErrorCode` union) + copy under `errors.actions.*` in each app's `messages/*.json`.
- Result type: `ActionResult<T>`; check with `isActionFailure`; log with `logActionFailure(context, err)`.
- Client resolves with `resolveActionError(tErrors, result.error)`; success → `showActionSuccess`.

## Data conventions

- **Server state = TanStack Query. Client/UI state = Zustand** (`'use client'` only). Realtime = stamp queue + disputes only.
- **RLS on every table before writing queries.** Service-role client only for privileged server paths.
- Supabase types: **`packages/supabase/src/types.ts` is the hand-maintained source of truth** (strict unions mirror check constraints). `pnpm supabase:types` writes raw CLI output to the gitignored `types.generated.ts` — diff it and merge new columns/tables into `types.ts` by hand. See `packages/supabase/AGENTS.md`.

## i18n

- Every user-facing string (labels, errors, `aria-*`) via `next-intl`. Keys in `apps/<app>/messages/{en,ne,fi}.json`. `en.json` is source of truth; `ne`/`fi` must reach key parity (see Day 11).

## Commands

```sh
pnpm build | pnpm lint | pnpm check-types        # all apps (turbo)
pnpm exec turbo <task> --filter=customer          # single app
pnpm supabase:types                               # write raw types.generated.ts to diff against types.ts
pnpm exec supabase db push                        # apply migrations to linked project
```

## Migrations

- Location `supabase/migrations/`; naming `YYYYMMDDHHMMSS_v2_<slug>.sql`. Include RLS in the same migration.

